[FEN "8/8/6P1/8/4k1BK/r3p3/6P1/8 b - - 0 55"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/8/6P1/8/4k1BK/r3p3/6P1/8_b_-_-_0_55"]

{ Just a bishop against his rook today. Your g pawn is nearly home, and only one order of moves gets it there. }
55... Ra5 { The rook swings across to stop your pawn. [%csl Ra5] } 56. g7 { Yes. The pawn drags his rook to the one square your bishop can see. [%csl Ga8] } (56. Bf3+ { The right idea at the wrong moment. His rook is not on the diagonal yet. } 56... Kf4 { He steps up, your pawn is still stuck, and it is a draw. [%csl Rg6] }) (56. g3 { A quiet pawn move that does nothing for the runner. } 56... Ra1 { The rook swings behind and the pawn never moves again. Drawn. }) (56. Bf5+ { A check that throws the bishop away. } 56... Kxf5 { Simply taken, and now you are the one who is lost. [%cal Re4f5] }) (56. Kg3 { Bringing the king back to help the pawn. } 56... Rg5 { The rook pins your bishop to your king and wins it. You are lost. [%cal Rg5g3] }) (56. Bh5 { Guarding the pawn from behind. } 56... Rxh5+ { He gives the rook for the bishop and the pawn falls too. Drawn. [%cal Ra5h5] }) 56... Ra8 { a8 is the only square that stops the pawn, so there it sits. } 57. Bf3+ { Check! He has to answer, and your bishop looks straight through to a8. [%cal Gf3a8] } (57. Kg5 { Walking the king up to escort the pawn. } 57... Rb8 { The rook waits on the eighth rank for ever. Drawn. }) (57. Be2 { Stepping aside to let the pawn run. } 57... Rg8 { The rook parks in front of it. You are lost. [%csl Rg8] }) (57. Bf5+ { A check, but the bishop is what you are giving away. } 57... Kxf5 { Your bishop is gone for nothing, and his rook still sits on a8 watching the square. Nothing is left to fight him for it. You are lost. [%cal Re4f5] }) (57. Bh5 { Guarding from the other side. } 57... Rg8 { The same answer, and your pawn is dead. You are lost. [%csl Rg8] }) 57... Kd4 { He steps away from the check. } 58. Bxa8 { The rook is yours, and a bishop with two pawns is an army against his lone king and pawn. [%csl Ga8][%tail] } (58. Kg5 { Escorting the pawn instead of taking the rook. } 58... Rb8 { He holds the eighth rank and you can never push. Drawn. }) (58. Bg4 { Tucking the bishop away to g4 and letting his rook live on a8. } 58... Rg8 { Now the rook stops the pawn dead. You are lost. [%csl Rg8] }) (58. Be4 { Offering a trade you cannot afford. } 58... Kxe4 { The bishop is gone. You are lost. [%cal Rd4e4] }) 58... e2 59. g8=Q 59... e1=Q+ 60. Kh3 { Your king tucks into the corner, safe, and a queen with a bishop in support beats a lone queen every time. That is winning. } 1-0


