[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/3k4/8/2pb4/7R/1p2K3/8/1PP1nP2/8_b_-_-_0_43"]

{ A new theme: two minor pieces take on a lone rook. Side by side they are strong, but easy prey the moment they drift apart. }
43... Nf4 { The knight jumps in and looks annoying. His two pieces are a long way apart. } 44. Rh6 { Nice. The rook takes the sixth rank and the bishop has to run. [%cal Gh6d6] } (44. Rh4 { Chasing the knight instead. } 44... Nd5 45. Kd4 Ke7 { The knight finds a home and the game is level. }) (44. Rh8+ { A check, but his king is happy to walk. } 44... Kc7 45. Rh7+ Kb6 { The checks run out and nothing has changed. Level. }) (44. Re5 { Offering a trade in the middle of the board. } 44... Bxe5 45. Kxe5 Nd5 { He swaps with pleasure. Level. }) (44. Rf5 { Attacking the knight, but it simply steps away. } 44... Ne6 45. Rf6 Ke7 { Both his pieces are safe. Level. }) 44... Bf8 { The bishop runs to the corner, and his pieces are still apart. } 45. Rf6 { The f file attacks the bishop and the knight at once. He can save one. [%cal Gf6f8,Gf6f4] } (45. Rxc6 { A free pawn. But now his pieces get to breathe. } 45... Kd7 46. Rf6 Ne6 { The knight is safe and the win has gone. Level. }) (45. Kxf4 { You take the knight, and he takes more. } 45... Bxh6+ { Your rook is gone. Now you are lost. [%cal Rf8h6] }) (45. Ke5 { The king marches into the middle, straight past a hanging rook. } 45... Bxh6 { Same problem: the rook was hanging. You are lost. }) (45. Rh8 { Retreating to safety and giving him a free move. } 45... Ne6 46. Kf5 Kd7 { Both pieces are fine again. Level. }) 45... Bg7 { He saves the bishop, and it attacks your rook on the way. } 46. Rxf4 { The knight is yours. A rook and three pawns against a bishop and two. Winning. [%csl Gf4] } (46. Rxc6 { The pawn again, but the knight was the bigger prize. } 46... Nh3 47. f4 Bxb2 { He wriggles out of everything. Level. }) (46. Rf8+ { A check that hands over your rook. } 46... Bxf8 { Your rook is simply gone, traded away for nothing you needed. You are lost. [%cal Rg7f8] }) (46. Kf5 { Defending the rook with the king. } 46... Bxf6 47. Kxf6 Kd7 { You traded rook for bishop and his knight lives. You are lost. }) 1-0


