[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/8/8/5kp1/RP3n2/6K1/3n1P1P/8_w_-_-_1_41"]

{ Your two knights and a pawn have to deal with a rook that has wandered off to escort his own passed pawn. }
41. b5 { The pawn runs, and his rook is a long way from his own king. [%csl Rg3] } 41... Nf1+ { Check! His king has exactly one square, and it is the one you want. [%cal Gf1g3] } (41... Ne2+ { The other knight checks. } 42. Kg2 Ne4 43. b6 { His pawn runs and yours does not. You are lost. }) (41... Nh5+ { A check from the other side. } 42. Kg2 Ne4 43. b6 { Same story. The b pawn queens and you are lost. }) (41... Ne4+ { A fork, and he is delighted to take it. } 42. Rxe4 Kxe4 43. b6 { The rook goes but the pawn queens. You are lost. [%cal Ra4e4] }) (41... Nd5 { Trying to block the pawn. } 42. Rd4 Ne4+ 43. Rxe4 { The rook is quicker than two knights. You are in real trouble. }) (41... Nd3 { The knight sits down in front of the pawn instead of giving check. } 42. b6 Nc5 43. Ra5 { Nothing stops that pawn. You are lost. }) 42. Kf3 { The only square he had. } 42... g4# { Mate! The little pawn does it, with both knights and your king covering the rest. [%csl Ge3,Gg3,Ge2,Gg2] } (42... Nxh2+ { A free pawn with check, and mate was sitting there. } 43. Ke3 Ng4+ 44. Kf3 { You have a pawn, he still has a rook. Level. }) (42... Nd2+ { Another check, but this one goes nowhere. } 43. Ke3 Nb3 44. Ra3 { His rook takes over the board. You are worse. }) (42... Ng3 { Blocking your own mate. } 43. Rxf4+ gxf4 44. fxg3 { Everything falls apart. You are lost. }) (42... Ke5 { The king wanders off. } 43. b6 Nxh2+ 44. Kg3 { The pawn queens. You are lost. }) 0-1


