{ Bishop, knight and a passed pawn are on your side today, and his lone rook cannot watch all of it at once. }
43... Ke6 { His king hurries across to help. Every move but one throws the win away. } 44. c7 { Yes. Now his rook must drop to c2 to stop it, and c2 is not a safe square. [%cal Gc7c8] } (44. Nd4+ { The fork, one move too early. His rook is not on c2 yet. } 44... Kd6 45. Ba4 Rd2 { The knight has to move again and you are lost. }) (44. Nc5+ { A check, but it does nothing about the rook. } 44... Kd6 45. Ne4+ Kc7 { His king reaches your pawn. You are lost. }) (44. f5+ { A free check. } 44... Kd6 45. Nc5 Rc2 { The pawn falls anyway and you are lost. }) (44. Bc4+ { Another check with nothing behind it. } 44... Kd6 45. Nd4 Rd2 { One move too slow. You are lost. }) (44. Be2 { Blocking his runner on f3. } 44... fxe2+ { The pawn eats your bishop. You are lost. [%cal Rf3e2] }) 44... Rc2 { He has to stop the pawn, and c2 is the only square that does it. } 45. Nd4+ { The fork! Check on the king and a hit on the rook, both from d4. [%cal Gd4e6,Gd4c2] } (45. c8=Q { A new queen on c8! But his rook on c2 has been watching that square up the column all along. [%cal Rc2c8] } 45... Rxc8 { Simply taken, and you are lost. [%cal Rc2c8] }) (45. Bd3 { Attacking the rook with the bishop instead. } 45... Rxc7 { He gives nothing and takes your pawn. You are lost. }) (45. Bc6 { Blocking the file with the bishop. } 45... Rxc6 { He takes it and your pawn falls next. You are lost. [%cal Rc2c6] }) (45. Nd2 { Defending the f3 pawn from behind. } 45... Rxc7 { The pawn is gone and so is your game. You are lost. }) 45... Kd6 { He saves the king. } 46. Nxc2 { The rook is yours, and even if he scoops a pawn or two back, a bishop and a knight together are still far too much for him. [%csl Gc2] } (46. Nf5+ { A second check instead of taking. } 46... Kxc7 { He eats the pawn and keeps the rook. You are lost. }) (46. Bd3 { Hitting the rook one more time. } 46... Rc1+ 47. Kf2 Kxc7 { Check first, pawn second. You are much worse. }) (46. Be8 { Tucking the bishop out of the way. } 46... Rc1+ 47. Kf2 Kxc7 { The same escape. You are lost. }) 1-0


