{ A new theme: giving material away. What you get for it does not have to be material. }
69. Rxc1 { He takes your rook, and his pawn is two steps from home. [%csl Rg6] } 69... Nxc1 { Of course. Now his pawn runs, and there is nothing at all you can do about it. } 70. g7 { It cannot be stopped, and it queens next move. Is there anything faster? } 70... Nb3 { The quiet move! The knight is heading for a square his king cannot cover. } (70... Ne2 { The other quiet square. So close. } 71. g8=Q { The queen appears and there is no mate. Only a draw. }) (70... Bd4 { Attacking the pawn at last. } 71. g8=Q { Too late. The queen arrives and you are lost. }) (70... Ke3 { He marches his king in, hoping to help, but the queen is coming regardless. } 71. g8=Q { Your net is not built yet. You are lost. }) (70... Nd3 { Another knight square, and it does not do the job. } 71. g8=Q { His queen arrives all the same, and that knight move bought you nothing. You are lost. }) 71. g8=Q { He gets his queen. } 71... Nd2# { Mate! There is a queen on the board and she cannot save him. Two pieces did that. [%csl Gd2] } (71... Nd4 { A good square, but not the square. } 72. Qf8+ { Her majesty starts checking and you are lost. }) (71... Be3 { Setting up slowly. } 72. Qxb3 { The knight simply falls. You are lost. [%cal Rg8b3] }) (71... Ke4 { Stepping away instead. } 72. Qxb3 { The new queen just eats your knight. You are lost. [%cal Rg8b3] }) 0-1


